## {{lb|en|physics|of a [[ferromagnetic]] material}} Having the capability of being a permanent magnet by being a material with high magnetic [[coercivity]] (compare [[soft]]).
## {{lb|en|physics|of [[electromagnetic]] [[radiation]]}} Having a high [[energy]] (high [[frequency]]; short [[wavelength]]).
##: {{ux|en|'''hard''' X-rays}}
## {{lb|en|photography|of light}} Made up of [[parallel]] [[ray]]s, producing clearly defined [[shadow]]s.
# {{lb|en|personal or social}} Having a severe property; presenting difficulty.
## Difficult or requiring a lot of [[effort]] to do, understand, experience, or deal with.
##: {{ux|en|a '''hard''' problem;&emsp; a '''hard''' question;&emsp; a '''hard''' topic}}
##* {{quote-text|en|year=1988|title=An Oracle|author=w:Edmund White
|passage=Ray found it '''hard''' to imagine having accumulated so many mannerisms before the dawn of sex, of the sexual need to please, of the staginess sex encourages or the tightly capped wells of poisoned sexual desire the disappointed must stand guard over.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-07-26|author=[http://www.theguardian.com/profile/nick-miroff Nick Miroff]| volume=189| issue=7| page=32| magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly| title=[http://www.theguardian.com/world/2013/jul/23/mexico-insect-cuisine-sustainable-food Mexico gets a taste for eating insects&nbsp;&hellip;]| passage=The San Juan market is Mexico City's most famous deli of exotic meats, where an adventurous shopper can hunt down '''hard'''-to-find critters such as ostrich, wild boar and crocodile.}}
